# Principal Forward Deployed DevOps Engineer

## Overview

We are looking for a **Principal Forward Deployed DevOps Engineer** to work directly with teams building and running services on our strategic platforms.

This is a senior, hands-on role. The person in this post will embed with delivery teams, help them use shared platforms effectively, and step into difficult technical problems where platform adoption, delivery and operational reality meet.

This is not a central advisory role and it is not architecture at a distance. It is for someone who can work closely with teams, understand what is slowing them down, and fix it in practice.

## What the role is for

The purpose of this role is to help teams succeed on strategic platforms by providing deep, hands-on engineering support where it is most needed.

That means:
- working directly with teams adopting or running on shared platforms
- solving difficult platform, infrastructure and delivery problems in the open with those teams
- feeding recurring issues back into platform improvements, standards and better defaults
- helping close the gap between what the platform offers and what teams need in real delivery

## Key responsibilities

- Embed directly with teams using strategic platforms to help unblock delivery
- Provide hands-on support across infrastructure, CI/CD, cloud configuration, runtime issues and platform integration
- Help teams adopt platform patterns in a way that is practical, supportable and secure
- Troubleshoot difficult issues that sit between application teams and platform teams
- Identify where teams are struggling because of tooling, gaps in the platform, unclear standards or poor fit
- Turn repeated team problems into reusable fixes, clearer guidance or platform improvements
- Act as a senior technical engineer in high-friction or high-risk delivery situations
- Build trust with delivery teams by solving real problems, not just giving advice

## What we are looking for

We are looking for someone who:
- is operating at principal level
- is still strongly hands-on
- is comfortable embedding with teams rather than staying at arm’s length
- understands platforms from both sides: how they should work centrally, and what they feel like to use in delivery
- can deal with ambiguity, friction and technical complexity without becoming abstract or overly process-heavy

## Essential skills and experience

- strong hands-on DevOps or platform engineering background
- significant experience with cloud infrastructure and modern delivery practices
- experience working directly with delivery teams to solve technical problems
- strong understanding of CI/CD, infrastructure as code, runtime operations and service reliability
- ability to troubleshoot issues across team, platform and infrastructure boundaries
- strong judgement and the ability to operate independently in complex environments
- ability to turn practical delivery experience into improvements that scale beyond a single team

## What success looks like

Success in this role would look like:
- teams using strategic platforms are able to move faster and with less friction
- difficult adoption and delivery problems are resolved well
- recurring pain points are identified early and addressed properly
- teams have greater confidence in the platforms they are building on
- platform teams get better feedback grounded in real delivery experience
- the organisation gets stronger alignment between central platforms and the needs of product teams
